From cb4232d85a5347657e43316546034cdd6386b223 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 18:19:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: ipad5: Wake on the second Smart Cover hall
 sensor too

Only event 0x30 (PMIC GPIO line 0) was listed as a wake event, but that
is not the line iOS wakes on. At sleep entry AppleD2365PMU unmasks the
GPIO events of the lines whose configuration byte passes cfg & 0xc1 == 1
(sleep entry at 0xfffffff006bbb380). On a cold-booted J71t the boot
firmware leaves line 0 at 0x24 and line 10 at 0x25 (logged by the PMIC
GPIO driver, 2026-11-11), so iOS arms line 10 (event 0x3a) and not
line 0.

List both. The controller arms a wake-only event only while it stays
quiet after the latched events are dropped, so a sensor reading "open"
cannot end a sleep at once (both events were measured self-latching
with no cover on the iPad 6).

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s800x-ipad5.dtsi | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s800x-ipad5.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s800x-ipad5.dtsi
index 6c252bb..f7977c1 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s800x-ipad5.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s800x-ipad5.dtsi
@@ -190,8 +190,13 @@
 			interrupt-controller;
 			#interrupt-cells = <2>;
 			interrupts-extended = <&pinctrl_ap 76 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
-			/* Smart Cover front hall sensor (line 0): wake only. */
-			apple,wake-events = <0x30>;
+			/*
+			 * Smart Cover hall sensors (lines 0 and 10): wake only.
+			 * iOS arms line 10 for sleep (its boot configuration
+			 * 0x25 passes the sleep rule cfg & 0xc1 == 1; line 0's
+			 * 0x24 does not), so list both.
+			 */
+			apple,wake-events = <0x30 0x3a>;
 		};
 
 		tristar_charger: charger@180 {
